## Current Position

The Nami project has a **fully functional, standalone frontend Pomodoro timer** with an
ocean-themed design, background music, session history, todo list, and settings. All of
this runs client-side with no backend dependency. The original collaborative features
(auth, profiles, friends, rooms, WebSocket sync) were previously built as Django apps
and React pages, but have been **intentionally archived** to start fresh. The backend
shell (config, Docker, CI/CD) is still in place but has no active apps. The immediate
development situation is: either continue building the frontend independently, or begin
restoring archived backend apps and reconnecting the API layer.
